# Shell scripts must check out LF everywhere: a CRLF .sh breaks bash on
# Linux/WSL. Found via the field-agent plugin install smoke test — a fresh
# Windows clone (autocrlf) delivered templates/rest_api.sh with CRLF.
*.sh text eol=lf
# docs/runbooks/token-renewal.md pins these files by sha256, and the pins are for
# LF bytes. With core.autocrlf=true (rog-command) a checkout, stash or fresh
# clone would write them with CRLF, change every hash, and make the install
# steps that check the pins STOP. tools/tests/test_ssl_renewal.py checks this.
tools/renew_token.py text eol=lf
tools/*.ps1 text eol=lf
